# Obsidian vault (parity_vault)

Private project knowledge base. Open `parity_vault` as the Obsidian vault (not the repo root).

## What belongs here

- **What I've built:** architecture, stack, how it works, core concepts — mainly `Parity.md`
- **What I'm learning:** durable notes on multi-agent design, LLM APIs, evals, observability, debugging insights — new markdown notes under `parity_vault/`, linked from `Parity.md` when useful

## What does not belong here

- Changelogs, commit history, or automated sync from git
- Roadmaps / suggested improvements as a standing section
- Secrets (API keys, `.env`)
- Product/marketing fluff

## When editing code

- Keep `Parity.md` accurate if you change how the system works or move core files under `client/` / `server/`.
- Capture non-obvious learnings as vault notes; skip routine implementation noise.
- Leave `parity_vault/.obsidian/*` alone unless the user asks.
